I step outside the Mumbai airport.
It is the month of January.
But the air is not cold.
There is the smell of the sea in the air.
I look around.
There is a huge crowd here.
There is bright light everywhere.
My bags are heavy.
I am a little tired.
But I am very happy.
I need a taxi.
An attendant is standing there.
I go to him.
"Excuse me, where is the prepaid taxi counter?" I ask.
The attendant says, "Madam, the counter is straight ahead."
"Is it far?" I ask.
"No, it is to the right," he tells me.
"Thank you," I say.
I take my bags.
I walk towards the taxi counter.
